rooms_desc ({"This is the foyer of Wacko's huge, (and expensive), mansion.As you look around, you are amazed at how well decorated thisplace is. You realize how easilly you could get lost in herewithout a map! There is a door to the east, leading to the guestroom, and a great hall, opening up to the north.You also notice that there are two archways to the south, one tothe church, one to the shop in town. There is a board with noteson it between the two archways.","You are standing in the main hall of Wacko's mansion. On the wallsyou notice paintings of some of the most famous mages in the Holy Mission.Among them, Wuntvor and Lord Sith. They look frighteningly real! You seeseveral rooms off to the sides of the hall. To the north is Wacko's master bedroom, to the west you see a wood door, to the east you see astrange fire-like force field, and to the south, the main foyer.","Welcome to Wacko's guest room! Here you can relax, hang out, converse,trade weapons and armour, and share valuable quest information withthe host. There is a fully-stocked bar here, as well as a loadedentertainment center. You also notice several pieces of funitureneatly placed aroud the room. Off to the corner, your attention isdrawn to a dartboard. There is a picture on it that bears a strikingresembelance to Danseuse! You feel safe here, knowing that no monsterswould dare attack the Great Wacko in his own home!","This is the western end of a huge master bedroom. You see aking-sized bed up against the northern wall.The room is well lit due to the large bay window to the west. Theroom continues off to the east, and you feel warm air driftingin from the east.","This is where Wacko stores his items between game reboots. Thereare several shelves in here, on which lye dozens of objects arefar too complex for you to understand, but a few of them catch youreye. They have been placed on a table in the center of the room.Also, there is a staircase going downward to the east. But it is blocked by a strange, magical force.","This is where Wacko researches new, powerful spells. There are charts all over the walls, many magical items lying around, potions and flasks on the worktable, and a small crystal ballon the desk, which seems to be glowing with an intense, purplelight. There is a shelving unit on the far wall, which is stockedwith jars that contain such things as \"Eye of Chaosdemon\", and\"Blood of Affliction\". You see an archway to the north, and one tothe south. The archway to the south contains a closed door.","This is Wacko's library. There are shelves in this room which arestocked with hundreds of books with such names as \"Theories ofIllusionary Spell Casting\", \"Ethics Regarding Animation of the Dead\",and \"Lessons in Alteration Spells and Their Application in Combat\".There are also several overflowing scoll-racks against the far wall.Obviously, you think, Wacko is a well-read, well studied mage.","This is the easten part of the master bedroom. It is a well-lit area,due to the large number of windows in here. You also realize the source of the warm air. There is a huge fireplace built into theeastern wall of the room, and it contains a roaring fire.There is a large walk-in closet to the north, but is is locked-upright now. Also, you notice a love-seat in the center of theroom, where Wacko and Misticalla can sit down after a hard dayof questing and relax by the fire. You also notice a small tree ineach corner","This is where Wacko practices the spells that he studies, as wellas summoning creatures to battle. Sometimes he keeps creatures inhere to assist his adventuring and questing. As you look up, youcome to realize that the ceiling is just one gigantic skylight!You might want to get out of here soon. There is a knee-deep fog inhere which is glowing bright red and yellow. It's probably some unstableform of magic, perhaps a by-product of an experimental spell!","Of all the rooms in Wacko's House/Fortress, this is without a doubt,The strangest. Everything in this room is made out of black marble.You notice the smooth, polished marble is perfectly clean, and not ascuff mark is to be noticed anywhere! Along the walls you notice atleast twelve Archways, one on every wall. Some of the archways havedoors. Others have swirling mist, or glowing red and blue light in them,and appear to be magical in nature. Still others lead to tunnels whichwill bring you to various places in and aroud town. The only thing that they have in common is the fact that above each archway, a single word is etched in the marble, telling where it leads.",})
rooms_short ({"The Foyer","The Main Hall","The Guest Room","Western End of the Master Bedroom","The Storage Room","The Study","The Library","Eastern End of the Master Bedroom","The Summoning/Spell Room","The Portal/Teleporter Room",})
furnishings ({0,"","","","","","","","","",})
items ({({"A Sign","Please Don't enter the storage area! Thanks!   -Wacko",}),({"Paintings","These paintings look alive. You step back, out of fear!",}),({"dartboard","Try to hit danseuse","bar","One of these days, Wacko will hire a barkeeper!","entertainment center","A song is playing. \"Head Like a Hole\". Very, very loud!",}),({"bed","A large bed for two. It is covered by a canopy.","window","You can see the whole Holy Mission from here!",}),({"Table","This is where Wacko keeps his questing items.","Shelves","These shelves contain dozens of objects.",}),({"charts","They are written in some strange language. You don't understand them.","flasks","various flasks filled with tranparent, colored goop","shelves","The shelf looks ready to collapse under the weight of the many jars!",}),({"rack","It is filled with scrolls you don't understand",}),({"fire","A roaring fire. Don't get to close!","fireplace","A beautiful, marble fireplace","tree","A small, potted tree!",}),({"basket","It's empty! What a lousy shot Wacko must be!","desk","A large desk made of oak","chair","It looks very, very comfortable",}),({"Archways","There are several archways here. You wonder where they all lead.","Archway","There are several archways here. You wonder where they all lead.","Marble","Clean, unscuffed, black marble. It is polished and very smooth.",}),})
